   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening leadership</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australian Online Study Scholarship (AOSS) program provides opportunities to Samoan professionals who wish to complete a master degree but are unable to travel to Australia due to existing commitments at home. Scholars are supported with the provision of 97% of tuition fees and are required to maintain a part time load to enable to work and study concurrently. Australia&#x2019;s investment value for AOSS 2022 allows for 10 scholarships in this intake.
&#x200d;
During the reporting period, three graduates were supported under the AOSS program, and have completed postgraduate degrees in engineering management, public health, politics and policy to strengthen leadership capabilities. Graduates from this intake are currently employed in high priority sectors for the Government of Samoa: public service, engineering sector and private sector.</narrative>
    </description>
